# The factions of the freeroam mode (multiplayer, not in the original), read by src/faction/FactionDef.c. The six
# groups of data/modules/challenge.mod with their characters (the classes of the group), the class a member of each
# rank plays as, the pilot of its ships, the ship of each rank, the office (a level and an entity or dummy there where a
# player joins and leaves), the jail (where an arrested player or a member that died in the office level starts), the
# ranks (the deeds from which each rank starts), the relations to the other groups and the abilities (cooldown in
# seconds) in the order of the client's keys (join first).
# One statement per line, # starts a comment; "faction <Name>" starts the lines of a group.

# the wanted level of a player: the points from which levels 1..5 start
wanted 1 6 14 26 45
# points lost a second while the player's alarm is on, while it is off
decay 0.02 0.1
# points of a crime; the same crime of a player counts once in crimegap seconds
crime hurt_police 2
crime hurt_civilian 0.5
crime kill_police 8
crime kill_civilian 3
crime hurt_player 1
crime kill_player 6
crime theft 1.5
crimegap 1
# an arrest: the fine of the arrested player and the reward of the officer, per wanted level
fine 300
reward 150
# units from an officer to the wanted player it arrests: on foot, in a ship; from a player to the office's desk
reach 900 2000
deskreach 1200
# the siren: traffic within the radius moves away from the ship to the distance, held for the time (s)
siren 6000 4000 5
# backup outdoors: police ships of the wave type, so many; indoors the gears of the level chase the suspect
backup SPoli2_Rookie 2

# Bishops: sell life (life healed, the price the healed pays the healer), the green ray (damage, reach), revive (the s
# a dead player waits while a reviver is in the level, the units from the reviver to the body, the price)
heal 60 120
ray 30 2500
revive 15 900 100
# no player hurts another in a sanctuary: a level (*) or the radius around a dummy of a level
sanctuary Temple * 0
sanctuary Commercial DM_Door_Elevator_Temple 3000
# Bankers: steal (money, reach), suck (money from each player in front, reach), a loan (money, the debt per money
# loaned, the share of each income that pays it, the banker's commission), the bribe per wanted level dropped
steal 150 900
suck 60 1200
loan 1000 1.25 0.5 0.1
bribe 400
# the bank vault: in the level, at the dummy, it opens every so many s for so many s; the first player at it takes the
# money (a banker guards it: a deed; anyone else: a theft)
vault Bank DM_DesktopFunctionary_25 600 60 1500
# Mercs: a bounty (a placement, the most on one player, s until it ends), hired ships (model, count, s, price), the
# heavy loadout (life factor of the ship)
bounty 500 5000 3600
hire SMerc1 2 120 500
heavy 1.5
# Bureaucracy: the bullet time (radius, s, time speed inside), the bla-bla (radius, s asleep), permits (price, the rank
# from which a faction's ship needs one, the fine)
slow 2500 8 0.3
blabla 1200 4
permit 300 3 250
# Press: photos (reach, s a crime stays news, wanted points, reward), courier jobs (s, reward, bonus within half the
# time) to the desks of the routes
photo 4000 15 6 100
courier 300 400 200
route Police DM_DesktopFunctionary_00
route Temple DM_NPC_Repos_Bishop_04
route Bank DM_NPC_Repos_BankDirector_01
route TownHall DM_NPC_Repos_Functionary_54
route Press DM_NPC_Repos_Messenger_01
route GamblinDen DM_NPC_Spawn_MercenaryA_Smartie
# abilities of every player (after the keys of its faction while keys are left)
common bounty 30

